---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Azeruddin Sheikh — former Amazon ML Architect, now an independent production AI consultant. Seven years at Amazon, systems serving 2M+ requests/hour at 99.99%.">
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="shell grid-12" style="align-items:end;">
      <div style="grid-column: span 7;">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 class="display display--lg" style="margin-top:20px;">I have been the person <em>on call</em> for this.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Seven years as an ML architect at Amazon, leading a team of 20+ scientists and engineers. Before that, nine years in operations, programme management, and product. Now I fix production AI systems for mid-market software companies.
        </p>
        <p class="tiny" style="color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:14px;">
          You work with me directly. No account managers, no juniors, no handoff.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__actions" style="margin-top:24px;">
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SITE.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="me noopener">Connect on LinkedIn</a>
          <a class="link-arrow" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} style="font-size:13px;">{SITE.email}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="grid-column: 9 / span 4;">
        <figure class="portrait">
          <img
            src="/images/azeruddin-sheikh-portrait.jpg"
            alt="Azeruddin Sheikh, AI systems architect and former Amazon ML architect"
            width="896"
            height="1195"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
          <figcaption class="portrait__caption">
            <span>Azeruddin Sheikh<br />Chennai, India</span>
            <a href={SITE.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell grid-12" style="align-items:start;">
      <div style="grid-column: span 4;">
        <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
        <h2 class="display display--md" style="margin:18px 0 0;">Operator first. <em>Architect second.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div style="grid-column: 6 / span 7;">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I spent seven years as an ML architect and technical lead at Amazon. The systems I owned served <strong>two million requests an hour at 99.99% availability</strong>. On those systems I cut inference latency by 80%, built a classifier over 100,000+ classes that raised accuracy by 35% and halved processing time, and delivered more than $20M in savings.
          </p>
          <p>
            Before the ML years, I spent nine years in Amazon operations, programme management, and product. That matters more than it sounds. It means I design for the person doing the work and for the cost of running the system, not just for the benchmark.
          </p>
          <p>
            I have sat on both sides. I have been the person who has to make a system work at scale, and the person who has to explain to a business why it is not working yet. I know what vendors leave out because I have had to fix what they left out.
          </p>
          <p>
            You get me, not a delivery team. The person who scopes the diagnostic is the person who does the work, and the person you can reach while it is running.
          </p>

          <h2>Why independent</h2>
          <p>
            I do not sell software. I do not take referral fees from vendors. I do not have a partner programme. Where the right answer is a product you buy without me, I say so — in writing, in a document you keep, so you can hold me to it later.
          </p>
          <p>
            A recommendation from someone who profits either way is worth less than the paper it is printed on. That is the entire reason this practice is structured the way it is.
          </p>

          <h2>How I work</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Diagnose the whole stack.</strong> Data and retrieval, model and inference, orchestration and evals. Most production failures are not prompt problems.</li>
            <li><strong>Fix the highest-leverage problem first.</strong> One change that moves cost, latency, or reliability, measured against a baseline agreed before the work starts.</li>
            <li><strong>Ship with evals, guardrails, and observability.</strong> A system that fails loudly, names its failures, and can be operated by your team without me.</li>
            <li><strong>Hand off with runbooks.</strong> Written architecture decisions, cost model, failure modes, and on-call notes. Your team keeps the code.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>What I do not do</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Hourly billing, staff augmentation, or body shopping.</li>
            <li>Free discovery calls, free proposals, or free proofs of concept.</li>
            <li>Generic AI strategy with no access to systems or data.</li>
            <li>Publish client results or testimonials before a client has approved them.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Location and availability</h2>
          <p>
            I am based in Chennai, India, with an 8–11am ET overlap. I have worked with US teams for 16 years. If daily onsite presence is required, I am not the right fit — and I will say so before you buy anything.
          </p>
          <p>
            I keep the practice small — a handful of engagements at a time — so the person who scopes the work is the person who does it. If the timing does not fit, I will tell you rather than take the work and subcontract it.
          </p>
          <p>
            References from former Amazon colleagues are available on request, labelled as professional references rather than client testimonials. I sign NDAs, I do not train on client data, and I work inside your environment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout-box" style="margin-top:36px;">
          <p class="mono" style="font-size:10px;color:var(--color-accent-deep);margin:0 0 10px;">The proof bar</p>
          <p style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.4vw,1.9rem);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.02em;">
            {SITE.proofBarLong}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="shell grid-12" style="align-items:end;">
      <div style="grid-column: span 7;">
        <p class="eyebrow">Work with me</p>
        <h2 class="display display--md" style="margin:18px 0 20px;">Start with the diagnosis, not a call.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The diagnostic is two weeks and $12,500. It tells you what is broken, what it costs, and what to do first — whether or not you hire me for the next part.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="grid-column: 9 / span 4; display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/contact#diagnostic">Start a diagnostic — $12,500</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SITE.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
